  fullName     String
  username     String  @unique
  email        String?
  phone        String?
  passwordHash String

  /// MUST SET A NEW PASSWORD BEFORE DOING ANYTHING ELSE (3 Oct 2026).
  ///
  /// Set when an administrator resets somebody's password. Atlas generates a
  /// strong one, shows it to the admin ONCE, and flags the account - so the
  /// temporary password the admin read out works exactly long enough to get in
  /// and is then replaced by one only that person knows.
  ///
  /// This exists because the request was to let admins SEE each employee's
  /// password, which is not possible and should not be: `passwordHash` is a
  /// one-way scrypt fingerprint, so there is no password stored to show, and
  /// storing one reversibly would mean a single database leak handed over every
  /// employee's password - which people reuse on their bank. The real problem
  /// was that an admin had to invent and type a password every time, and that
  /// is what this solves, without anything readable ever being stored.
  mustChangePassword Boolean @default(false)

  /// When the password was last set, by anyone. On the users screen so an admin
  /// can see at a glance who is still using one an admin chose for them.
  passwordSetAt DateTime?

  /// Wrong passwords in a row; 5 locks sign-in for 15 minutes (auth/staff-password.ts).
  /// The person's id in a migrated source system ("LEGACY_USER:<id>" for Vcare), so
  /// old records that name them by that id show their name (health check I1).
